<title>GERMANY: German DGB union says April unemployment to drop.</title>
<headline>German DGB union says April unemployment to drop.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pan-German unemployment will show a slight decline of 100,000 to 150,000, before seasonal adjustment, in April from the month before, the DGB trades union federation said on Friday.</p>
<p>Ursula Engelen-Kefer said April unadjusted unemployment is still likely to be above 4.3 million, compared with 4.477 million in March.</p>
<p>Engelen-Kefer is on the board of the Federal Labour Office.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
